    "scope": "One YAML document from a bounded local byte buffer composed by libyaml's loader into a yaml_document_t node graph; schema-neutral YAML 1.2 control subset only",
    "family": "libyaml (reader.c/scanner.c/parser.c/loader.c)",
    "family_note": "Own C scanner, event parser and composer. The same libyaml family sits under PyYAML's CLoader/CSafeLoader, PHP PECL ext-yaml, Ruby Psych (the controls' cross-check) and, as a c2rust translation, Rust unsafe-libyaml/serde_yaml; those paths are not independent evidence for this one.",
    "typing_caveat": "libyaml returns every scalar as text with its style and the default tag; it does not resolve plain scalars to types. The harness types plain scalars with the YAML 1.2 core-schema patterns (null, bool, int, float, otherwise str) and every quoted or block scalar as str. Structure, escapes, block-scalar folding and chomping, document markers and alias expansion come from libyaml; the int/float/bool/null distinction is adapter-side.",
